Document.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. This Project will be completed at Building FF10 (Normandy Hall, 346 Ontario Street). The project area will include the existing parking lot and adjacent drainage swales.

Project work will include, but is not limited to:


	Removal of existing asphalt;
	Raising and adjusting the grade (elevation) throughout the lot and perimeter to eliminate ponding water, including adjusting a minor surface collection swale, which will direct surface flows through the existing vegetated areas to the water;
	Restore and improve existing rip-rap (aggregate) discharge areas within the existing fenceline;
	Remove and replace concrete curbs, gutters and sidewalks within the lot;
	Install new light standards and replace existing light standards within the asphalt lot;
	Install new asphalt and restore all disturbed areas.


It is expected that all work under the Project will be completed within the fenced property boundary; this work is not expected to include in water works or impacts to the top and/or sides of the adjacent shoreline. The Project is required as the conditions of the existing parking lot are poor; additionally, current elevations are ineffective at managing overland flow, which leads to ponding of water within the parking lot during wet conditions and a risk to existing infrastructure. Improvements will decrease the accumulation of water on the asphalt surface to maximize the number of vehicles that can use the lot for parking. Inadequate existing lighting concerns were raised, and this project also aims to improve the lighting throughout the lot. The goal of this project is to provide a safe, modern, and sustainable parking facility that meets current and future operational needs. Project objectives include improving vehicle and pedestrian safety, enhancing stormwater management, reducing maintenance requirements, and improving energy efficiency with LED lighting to support DND&#39;s long-term sustainability goals. The completed project will deliver a durable and efficient parking lot that enhances user experience, aligns with accessibility and environmental standards, and supports the Department&#39;s energy and modernization initiatives.

&nbsp;

Document.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Ce projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; au b&acirc;timent FF10 (b&acirc;timent Normandie, 346, rue Ontario). La zone vis&eacute;e par les travaux comprendra le terrain de stationnement actuel et les foss&eacute;s de drainage adjacents.

Les travaux &agrave; effectuer sont, entre autres, les suivants :


	Enl&egrave;vement de l&#39;asphalte;
	&Eacute;l&eacute;vation de la pente dans l&#39;ensemble du stationnement et de son p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre afin d&#39;&eacute;liminer les accumulations d&#39;eau, ce qui comprend l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un petit foss&eacute; dirigeant les &eacute;coulements de surface vers le plan d&#39;eau &agrave; travers la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation existante;
	Remise en &eacute;tat et am&eacute;lioration des zones de d&eacute;versement en enrochement (granulats) existantes situ&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre;
	Enl&egrave;vement et remplacement des bordures, des goutti&egrave;res et des trottoirs en b&eacute;ton dans le stationnement;
	Emplacement des lampadaires sur la surface asphalt&eacute;e du stationnement;
	Installation d&#39;asphalte neuf et remise en &eacute;tat de toutes les zones perturb&eacute;es.


Tous les travaux devraient &ecirc;tre ex&eacute;cut&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur des limites du terrain cl&ocirc;tur&eacute;. Aucun travail dans l&#39;eau n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu et aucune partie du rivage ne devrait &ecirc;tre touch&eacute;e. Ces travaux sont n&eacute;cessaires, &eacute;tant donn&eacute; le mauvais &eacute;tat actuel du terrain de stationnement. En outre, les pentes actuelles ne permettent pas un &eacute;coulement efficace des eaux de surface, ce qui cause des accumulations d&#39;eau dans le stationnement en temps de pluie et repr&eacute;sente un risque pour l&#39;infrastructure existante. Les am&eacute;liorations apport&eacute;es permettront de r&eacute;duire les accumulations d&#39;eau sur la surface asphalt&eacute;e et de maximiser ainsi le nombre de v&eacute;hicules pouvant se stationner. Ce projet vise &eacute;galement &agrave; am&eacute;liorer l&#39;&eacute;clairage dans l&#39;ensemble du stationnement en r&eacute;ponse aux pr&eacute;occupations ayant &eacute;t&eacute; soulev&eacute;es &agrave; ce sujet. Le but de ce projet est d&#39;offrir un terrain de stationnement s&eacute;curitaire, moderne et durable qui r&eacute;pond aux besoins op&eacute;rationnels actuels et futurs. Ce projet vise notamment l&#39;am&eacute;lioration de la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des v&eacute;hicules et des pi&eacute;tons, l&#39;am&eacute;lioration de la gestion des eaux de ruissellement, la r&eacute;duction des besoins en entretien et l&#39;augmentation de l&#39;efficacit&eacute; &eacute;nerg&eacute;tique gr&acirc;ce &agrave; un &eacute;clairage DEL afin d&#39;assurer la r&eacute;alisation des objectifs du MDN en mati&egrave;re de durabilit&eacute;. Aux termes des travaux, on disposera d&#39;un terrain de stationnement durable et efficient qui am&eacute;liorera l&#39;exp&eacute;rience des utilisateurs, sera conforme aux normes en mati&egrave;re d&#39;accessibilit&eacute; et d&#39;environnement et contribuera aux initiatives du Minist&egrave;re en mati&egrave;re d&#39;&eacute;nergie et de modernisation.

&nbsp;

